From: Ramesh Goswami <ramesh@listenfirstmedia.com>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 11:02:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Talent Social Media Finder: identity-anchor resolver + Flask
 service

Resolves talent/influencer social handles by identity anchor rather than by
name string, which is what makes same-name collisions tractable.

- platforms.py    URL -> (platform, handle) for FB/IG/X/YT/Wikipedia/IMDb/TikTok/LinkedIn
- authorities.py  31 authorities mapped to Wikidata P-numbers (hub-and-spoke)
- aggregators.py  22 link-in-bio hosts, __NEXT_DATA__/JSON-LD extractors, reverse cascade
- evidence.py     5-tier evidence model; a name match alone can never resolve
- resolver.py     pipeline + SQLite entity store, collision registry, provenance
- fetcher.py      cached, rate-limited, allowlisted HTTP adapter
- app.py          Flask service, demo mode by default

68/68 offline tests pass. Not yet verified against live endpoints.
